From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Julien Etienne <julien.etienne@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 12:44:28 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 622/622] phy: mediatek: DIAGNOSTIC also dump the USB11
 endpoint 0 windows

Print the frame number, INDEX, and endpoint 0's registers in both the
indexed window at 0x10 and the flat window at 0x100, to show which of
the two the MT6797 USB11 controller implements and whether it sends
frames. Still read-only; the FIFOs are not read.
---
 drivers/phy/mediatek/phy-mtk-usb11-dump.c | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/phy/mediatek/phy-mtk-usb11-dump.c b/drivers/phy/mediatek/phy-mtk-usb11-dump.c
index c4dbb0ed0..ba482b18c 100644
--- a/drivers/phy/mediatek/phy-mtk-usb11-dump.c
+++ b/drivers/phy/mediatek/phy-mtk-usb11-dump.c
@@ -60,6 +60,15 @@ static int __init usb11_dump_init(void)
 	for (i = 0; i < ARRAY_SIZE(mac_regs); i++)
 		pr_info("usb11-dump: mac %-11s: %02x\n", mac_regs[i].name,
 			readb(mac + mac_regs[i].off));
+	pr_info("usb11-dump: mac Frame      : %04x\n", readw(mac + 0x0c));
+	pr_info("usb11-dump: mac Index      : %02x\n", readb(mac + 0x0e));
+	/* Endpoint 0 in the indexed window and in the flat one. */
+	for (i = 0; i < 0x10; i += 4)
+		pr_info("usb11-dump: mac idx+%02x    : %08x\n", i,
+			readl(mac + 0x10 + i));
+	for (i = 0; i < 0x10; i += 4)
+		pr_info("usb11-dump: mac flat0+%02x  : %08x\n", i,
+			readl(mac + 0x100 + i));
 
 	iounmap(mac);
 	iounmap(phy);
